  "summary": "I build and steward engineering systems and infrastructure that Windows and Azure depend on to operate securely and reliably at scale.\n \nOver more than a decade at Microsoft, my work has focused on secure build platforms, software supply‑chain integrity, network isolation, and resilience engineering, particularly in areas where failures would have broad business or customer impact.\n \nA core theme of my experience is security‑driven resilience: identifying and addressing scenarios where trust assumptions degrade, infrastructure becomes constrained, or dependencies fail and ensuring critical build and release workflows continue to operate safely and correctly. This includes contributions to Windows Dialtone, where the emphasis is on preserving business continuity for Windows and Azure build systems under catastrophic or degraded‑trust conditions.\n \nI’ve been a long‑term owner in Zero Trust Build and Network Isolation efforts, working across teams to translate evolving security and compliance requirements into durable engineering solutions that balance correctness, reliability, and developer productivity.\n \nFrom 2023–2025, I served as an engineering manager, which strengthened my ability to scale impact through others, delegate ownership, and communicate clearly with leadership. Today, I operate as a senior‑level IC and tech lead, driving cross‑team alignment, architectural decisions, and risk tradeoffs across organizational boundaries.\n \nI’m most effective in roles that require deep system context, long‑term ownership, and judgment under ambiguity, especially where security, infrastructure, and platform scale intersect.",
